"Pipe Pressure Drop Calculation (Colebrook-White Equation)

Calculates the friction pressure drop in a straight pipe using the Colebrook-White
correlation. Working fluid: n-pentane (both gas and liquid conditions shown).

Inputs:
  - Pipe inner diameter D_i
  - Absolute roughness epsilon
  - Mass flow rate M_dot
  - Pipe length L = 10 m

Outputs:
  - Pressure drop DELTAP [Pa] and DELTAPbar [bar]
  - Dynamic pressure P_dyn
"
fluid$='n-pentane'{'R123'}
epsilon=0.0000015 [m] "absolute roughness"
D_i=16E-3 [m] "inner diameter"

"n-pentane conditions"
	"gas phase"
{P=10E5
T=T_sat+50}

	"liquid phase"
P=1E5
T=T_sat+10

T_sat=T_sat(fluid$,P=P)
v=volume(fluid$,P=P,T=T)
rho=1/v
M_dot=80E-3 [kg/s]


"pipe friction factor (Colebrook-White)"

1/sqrt(f)=-2*LOG10(epsilon/(3.7*D_i)+2.51/(Re*sqrt(f))) "colebrook"
f_vlad=(-1.8*log10((6.9/Re+(epsilon/(3.7*D_i))^1.11)))^(-2)

"friction pressure gradient [Pa/m]"
deltaP_lin=f/D_i*rho*U^2/2 "[Pa/m]"
deltaP_lin_vlad=f_vlad/D_i*rho*U^2/2 "[Pa/m]"
U=V_dot/A_i
A_i=PI*D_i^2/4
V_dot=M_dot*v

"Re"
Re=D_i*U/nu
nu=mu/rho
mu=viscosity(fluid$,P=P,T=T)

"total pressure drop"

DELTAP=deltaP_lin*L "[Pa]"
DELTAP_vlad=deltaP_lin_vlad*L "[Pa]"
L=10 [m]
DELTAPbar=DELTAP/1E5 "[bar]"
DELTAP_vladbar=DELTAP_vlad/1E5 "[bar]"

"dynamic pressure"

P_dyn=rho*U^2/2
ratio=P_dyn/DELTAP

